				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Defer sky://terminal/create event to fix race condition\n\nThe terminal workbench's `LocalTerminalBackend.createProcess` flow has a timing vulnerability: when `sky://terminal/create` emits synchronously during step 1 (RPC in-flight), the Tauri event arrives before step 3 (`_ptys.set(id, pty)`) completes. This causes `_ptys.get(id)` to return `undefined`, skipping `handleReady` and preventing `processManager._onProcessReady` from firing. Since `ptyProcessReady` never resolves, every subsequent `processManager.write(data)` call hangs indefinitely—users see the terminal panel but all keystrokes are silently dropped.\n\nFix by emitting on a deferred tokio task with a 120ms delay, giving the RPC response roundtrip + `_ptys.set` sufficient headroom. Also switch to `LogSkyEmit` for visibility under `[DEV:SKY-EMIT]` histogram tracking.\n\nThis complements the existing `AppendTerminalOutput` replay buffer for data (added in c99ccbe), completing the terminal race-condition fix for both create and data events.",
			"SHA": "c2d0beca968f600d76ac4d85a436931124cfdf07"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T17:20:13Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Return integer id from localPty:createProcess\n\nThe VS Code terminal workbench expects `IPtyService.createProcess` to return a `Promise<number>` (the integer terminal id). However, Mountain was returning the full `{id, name, pid}` object. The workbench then keys its internal `_ptys` map by that object, so every `_ptys.get(<integer>)` lookup from `onProcessData`/`onProcessReady` returns `undefined`. This causes xterm to receive zero bytes even though Mountain's PTY reader emits data continuously—resulting in blank terminal panels.\n\nSplit the terminal handler into three distinct paths:\n- `localPty:spawn`: Preserves full response for Cocoon's Sky bridge\n- `localPty:createProcess`: Returns only the integer id per VS Code contract\n- `localPty:start`: No-op for eager-spawn pattern (shell already started during createProcess)\n\nThis fixes the terminal rendering while maintaining backward compatibility with existing spawn callers.",
			"SHA": "c99ccbe7715342838206eb2c54509fa3a97f513f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T16:59:58Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Simplify binary and product names\n\nRename the Mountain binary, library, and default-run targets from the verbose development profile name to simply \"Mountain\". This follows the project's PascalCase naming convention and removes the debug build artifact naming.\n\nIn tauri.conf.json, simplify the identifier from the lengthy development-specific string to \"land.editor.binary\" and the productName from the long debug name to \"Mountain\". Also remove the duplicate \"Binary/node\" entry from externalBin.\n\nThese changes clean up the build configuration for proper release builds while maintaining the same functionality.",
			"SHA": "db5f0f7bc58c4108ea4f51ec3ac0d30bb008def3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T16:55:25Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				3
			],
			"Message": "",
			"SHA": "f2b5c349377b143b33dab188478a947d77522a46"
		},
		{
